I've gotten to the point where Nethack is just a routine and winning
is 'easy'.  I've come up with a few ways to challenge myself during
the game, and wondered if there others out there with the same
problem (?)...
 
Method #1:  Play a Tourist or Archeologist and drop all your starting
            equipment.  Using any of it is against the rules.
            If you want to cheat a bit, pick one item to keep.
            Pets are allowed to help you, but for a further challenge
            you can desert him/her on level 1...
 
Method #2:  Stuff found 'laying around' in the dungeon is off
            limits and must be ignored.  The only equipment you can pick
            up and use has to be bought in shop.
 
Method #3:  Praying is against the rules for any reason.  This isn't
            TOO hard, but can be mildly challenging.  :)
 
Method #4:  Only hand to hand combat is allowed - literally!
            Weapons are off-limits.
 
Method #5:  Eating corpses is not allowed.  This is HARD in the
            later levels - there are ways to get most of the intrinsics,
            but it isn't very easy...
 
Any others?  I find games are more fun this way (and shorter!).  Method
#1 is particularly fun, I'm estatic when I get a 'find' like a dagger (I
have a weapon!  I have a weapon!).
 
